--- a/docs/data-cache.md
+++ b/docs/data-cache.md
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 ---

 # Data Cache
+
+Library settings allow 3, 4, or 5 books per row (9, 16, or 25 covers per page). Cover grid thumbnails are generated only for visible EPUB/XTC books and reused from their existing per-book disk caches. Books without covers use a placeholder; confirmed missing EPUB covers are remembered in `library-cover-missing`. Text files use a placeholder. Library opens the saved index on startup. After its first paint, a paced metadata-only check compares book paths, sizes, and modification timestamps with the saved index, then offers Refresh if they differ. Transfers and on-device file changes also offer Refresh. The check reads no book contents; edits retaining both size and timestamp may not be detected. No rebuild occurs until Refresh is selected unless the index is missing or incompatible. No cache format change or cache deletion is needed.

 CrossInk caches data aggressively on the SD card to minimize RAM use. The ESP32-C3 has about 380 KB of usable RAM, so rebuilding every book structure in memory on every open would be too expensive.

